@page "/guide"

<PageTitle>Guide · CleanProdHarden</PageTitle>

<h1>Guide</h1>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Why this tool exists</h2>
    <p>
        Migration <code>@DuplicateGroupLoader.HardenMigrationId</code> adds a unique filtered index on
        <code>Payments.EasyPayPaymentId</code>. It stops with error 51000 while two or more payments share a provider ID.
        This tool walks through every duplicate group, shows all the evidence, recommends an action, and applies the
        decision you approve. It uses the same rules, validations, and audit tables as
        <code>Migrations/Scripts/MergeDuplicateEasyPayPaymentIds.sql</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
        A group is every payment whose provider ID matches, ignoring case and trailing spaces. The group ID is the lowest
        payment ID in the group. The tool never calls EasyPay.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Workflow</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Enter your name in the sidebar. It is stored as <em>ApprovedBy</em> in the audit rows.</li>
        <li>Open <a href="groups">Groups</a>, or use <em>Next open group</em> on the dashboard.</li>
        <li>Read <em>What happened</em> and the recommendation. Compare the members side by side and check the donations, invoices, subscriptions, and raw rows.</li>
        <li>Choose an action and, for Reconcile, the owner. Edit the reason. Save, or Defer if you need more information.</li>
        <li>Run a <strong>dry run</strong>. It runs the real change in a transaction and rolls it back, so the database does not change.</li>
        <li>When applying is enabled, type the database name and <strong>Apply</strong>. The tool commits only the exact decision that passed the dry run.</li>
        <li>When the dashboard shows 0 duplicate groups, deploy the migration through the normal pipeline.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="hint">
        Applying is off by default. Enable it with <code>dotnet user-secrets set "CleanProdHarden:AllowApply" "true"</code> and restart.
        Decisions and history are stored in a local SQLite file (setting <code>CleanProdHarden:DecisionStorePath</code>), per server and database.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Actions</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
        <table class="table">
            <thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>What it does</th><th>Use it when</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Display.ActionLabel(ReconciliationAction.ReconcileIdentifiers)</td>
                    <td>@Display.ActionDescription(ReconciliationAction.ReconcileIdentifiers)</td>
                    <td>One payment really owns the provider ID, usually the payment confirmed by a Payed donation. Required when any member is confirmed.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Display.ActionLabel(ReconciliationAction.RetireIdentifier)</td>
                    <td>@Display.ActionDescription(ReconciliationAction.RetireIdentifier)</td>
                    <td>No member owns the ID, but you want to keep every row for history.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Display.ActionLabel(ReconciliationAction.DeleteGroup)</td>
                    <td>@Display.ActionDescription(ReconciliationAction.DeleteGroup)</td>
                    <td>Every member is an abandoned or superseded attempt with no money, no confirmation, and no referencing rows.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Safety checks on every run</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Each group runs in its own serializable transaction with <code>XACT_ABORT</code> and a 15-second lock timeout.</li>
        <li>The tool locks <code>Payments</code> exclusively and holds shared locks on <code>Donations</code> and <code>Invoices</code>, then evaluates the group again inside the transaction.</li>
        <li>The evidence hash must match the hash you reviewed. Any change to the group's rows rejects the run (51007).</li>
        <li>Audit rows are written before the change. Deleted rows are archived as JSON.</li>
        <li>Updated or deleted row counts must match the plan, and the provider ID must be unique afterwards.</li>
        <li>Each applied group gets a plan row in <code>EasyPayPaymentIdReconciliationPlans</code>, bound to this server and database.</li>
        <li>Apply requires a passing dry run of the same action, owner, reason, reviewer, and evidence.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="card">
    <h2>SQL decision rules</h2>
    <p class="hint">Evaluated in this order. The first rule that matches classifies the group.</p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
        <table class="table compact">
            <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (DecisionRule rule in Display.Rules)
                {
                    <tr><td class="mono">@rule</td><td>@Display.RuleDescription(rule)</td></tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Patterns</h2>
    <p class="hint">Patterns explain how a group probably came to exist. They refine the SQL rule and drive the recommendation.</p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
        <table class="table compact">
            <thead><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (GroupPattern pattern in Display.Patterns)
                {
                    <tr><td>@GroupPatternClassifier.Title(pattern)</td><td>@GroupPatternClassifier.Explanation(pattern)</td></tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Confidence</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
        <dt><span class="@Display.ConfidenceCss(RecommendationConfidence.High)">High</span></dt><dd>The SQL rules prove ownership or retirement safety.</dd>
        <dt><span class="@Display.ConfidenceCss(RecommendationConfidence.Medium)">Medium</span></dt><dd>The recommendation is safe, but confirm a business detail first.</dd>
        <dt><span class="@Display.ConfidenceCss(RecommendationConfidence.Low)">Low</span></dt><dd>Verify external evidence, such as the EasyPay back office, before deciding.</dd>
        <dt><span class="@Display.ConfidenceCss(RecommendationConfidence.None)">None</span></dt><dd>The evidence does not support an automatic recommendation.</dd>
    </dl>
</section>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Validation codes</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
        <table class="table compact">
            <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach ((int number, string meaning) in Codes)
                {
                    <tr><td class="mono">@number</td><td>@meaning</td></tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">Codes 51002–51013 match the SQL script. Codes from 51100 are specific to this tool.</p>
</section>

@code {
    private static readonly (int Code, string Meaning)[] Codes =
    {
        (ValidationCodes.ReasonOrOwner, "Missing reason, or the owner rules are violated."),
        (ValidationCodes.AuditHistoryExists, "Audit rows already exist for a payment in the group."),
        (ValidationCodes.DuplicatesRemain, "Duplicates remain after the action."),
        (ValidationCodes.ApprovalMissing, "The reviewer name is missing or too long."),
        (ValidationCodes.StaleEvidence, "The target or the group's evidence changed since the review."),
        (ValidationCodes.OwnerNotMember, "The owner is not a member of the group."),
        (ValidationCodes.MigrationRequirements, "Other migration requirements are violated (IDs over 50 characters, conflicting invoices)."),
        (ValidationCodes.UnsupportedAction, "No action, or an unsupported action."),
        (ValidationCodes.UnsafeDeletion, "Delete without safe deletion evidence for every member."),
        (ValidationCodes.DeletionDependencies, "Delete blocked by permissions, foreign keys, triggers, or referencing rows."),
        (ValidationCodes.RetireConfirmed, "Retire while a member is confirmed by a donation."),
        (ValidationCodes.TargetNotConfirmed, "The typed database name does not match the connected database."),
        (ValidationCodes.GroupNotFound, "The group no longer has duplicate provider IDs."),
        (ValidationCodes.RowCountMismatch, "An update or delete changed a different number of rows than planned."),
        (ValidationCodes.DryRunRequired, "Apply requires a passing dry run of the same decision."),
        (ValidationCodes.ApplyDisabled, "Applying is disabled in configuration."),
        (ValidationCodes.UnexpectedError, "SQL Server or the tool raised an unexpected error."),
    };
}
